### TITLE ###
format_epoch formats seconds in UTC
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss", tz="UTC"))
### STDOUT ###
2025-01-01 00:00:00

### TITLE ###
format_epoch auto-detects millis
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600123, "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss", tz="UTC"))
### STDOUT ###
2025-01-01 00:00:00

### TITLE ###
format_epoch respects explicit unit
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYY-MM-DD", unit="seconds", tz="UTC"))
### STDOUT ###
2025-01-01

### TITLE ###
format_epoch literal separators pass through
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYYMMDD-HHmmss", tz="UTC"))
### STDOUT ###
20250101-000000

### TITLE ###
format_epoch converts timezones
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm", tz="America/Chicago"))
### STDOUT ###
2024-12-31 18:00

### TITLE ###
format_epoch is the inverse of parse_date
### INPUT ###
t = parse_date("2026-03-22T14:30:00Z", tz="UTC")
print(format_epoch(t.epoch.seconds, "DD/MM/YYYY HH:mm", tz="UTC"))
### STDOUT ###
22/03/2026 14:30

### TITLE ###
format_epoch errors on ambiguous digit count
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(17356896001, "YYYY-MM-DD", tz="UTC"))
### STDERR ###
error[RAD20007]: Ambiguous epoch length (11 digits). Use 'unit' to disambiguate.
  --> <script>:1:7
  |
1 | print(format_epoch(17356896001, "YYYY-MM-DD", tz="UTC"))
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
   = info: rad docs RAD20007


### EXIT ###
1
### TITLE ###
format_epoch errors on invalid unit
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYY-MM-DD", unit="fortnights", tz="UTC"))
### STDERR ###
error[RAD30001]: Argument type 'str' is not assignable to expected type '["auto", "seconds", "millis", "micros", "nanos"]'
  --> <script>:1:51
  |
1 | print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYY-MM-DD", unit="fortnights", tz="UTC"))
  |                                                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
   = info: rad docs RAD30001


### EXIT ###
1
### TITLE ###
format_epoch errors on invalid timezone
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYY-MM-DD", tz="Mars/Olympus"))
### STDERR ###
error[RAD20009]: invalid time zone "Mars/Olympus"
  --> <script>:1:7
  |
1 | print(format_epoch(1735689600, "YYYY-MM-DD", tz="Mars/Olympus"))
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
   = info: rad docs RAD20009


### EXIT ###
1
### TITLE ###
format_epoch errors on empty format
### INPUT ###
print(format_epoch(1735689600, "", tz="UTC"))
### STDERR ###
error[RAD30003]: Cannot format epoch with an empty format string
  --> <script>:1:7
  |
1 | print(format_epoch(1735689600, "", tz="UTC"))
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
   = info: rad docs RAD30003


### EXIT ###
1
### TITLE ###
format_epoch errors are catchable
### INPUT ###
res = format_epoch(17356896001, "YYYY-MM-DD", tz="UTC") catch:
    print("caught")
### STDOUT ###
caught

